GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`may the proceeding be brought or the penalty imposed as if the repealing enactment had not been passed` `the day the question is about` `the enactment repeals another enactment` thing `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    `Article 17(2): the thing may be done as if the repealing enactment had not been passed` (`the text of the Law in force on` `the day the question is about`) `the enactment repeals another enactment` thing `a contrary intention appears`

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:82 | (3) The provisions of paragraph (2) shall apply in relation to an enactment which has expired in like manner as they apply in relation to an enactment which has been repealed.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 17(3), as it read before 28 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:82)
